  "body": "refactor(multiaxis): split first_traverse.rs along the domain seam\n\n## What moved where and why\n\n`crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse.rs` was 432 lines, over the\n400-line limit. The file held two concerns. The split follows the seam:\n\n- `first_traverse.rs` (now 320 lines) keeps the seam to the\n  first-traverse laws: which operations answer to them (`answers`,\n  `mill_order`, `newly_judged`, `newly_judged_on`), what they read over\n  (`Over`, `Turned`, `rides_of`, `rotaries_of`, `turned_axis`), the\n  rotary swept law (`judge_turned`), the verdict choreography (`judge`)\n  and the user-heights framing (`in_user_frame`).\n- `first_traverse_table.rs` (new, 131 lines) holds the 3+2 tilted-table\n  reading (#2987, #3081): `tilting_all`, `work_tilts`,\n  `table_top_face`, `TableRead`, `table_read`, `TABLE_UNJUDGED_NOTE`,\n  and the catalog table test. It has a one-line provenance comment.\n\nThe moved items are re-exported from `first_traverse`\n(`pub(super) use`), so every caller - `generate.rs`, `stamp.rs`,\n`rotary_traverse.rs`, `first_traverse_posed.rs` - keeps its paths and\nthe public API is stable. `operation/mod.rs` registers the new module.\n\n## Test count\n\n`#[test]` count in `crates/app` (src + tests): 4324 before, 4324 after.\nThe catalog table test moved with its code into the new module; no\ncoverage rode the split away.\n\n## Gate results\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on the final head: green.\nThe touched suites include `app:lib`, `app:first_traverse`,\n`app:first_traverse_table_tilt`, `app:first_traverse_posed`,\n`app:first_traverse_rotary`, `app:first_traverse_rotary_mill_turn`,\n`app:first_traverse_mill_turn` and the `camcraft-ui` suites that the\ngate map reaches - all pass. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app\n--all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo behaviour change is intended or exercised: this is a code move.\nNo heavy lane is reached by a pure move inside `crates/app/src/operation`.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nfork synced at v0.25.0\n\nFixes #3288\n",
